From: X710 bring-up <bringup@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: qcom: report the pogo pins' state when the TLMM probes

Every final state of these seven pins is known to match the stock kernel, and
every host-side variable that could be set has been excluded (tests 075-079).
What has never been looked at is the *transition*: what the bootloader leaves in
the pin control registers, and whether this probe or anything before it passes
through a state the keyboard's MCU never sees under stock.

Read-only, at probe, before any driver claims the pins: the control and IO
registers of gpio10, 12, 13, 62, 72, 75 and 106.
---
diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-msm.c b/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-msm.c
index 11db6564c..bb29115e6 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-msm.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-msm.c
@@ -1597,6 +1597,35 @@ int msm_pinctrl_probe(struct platform_device *pdev,
 		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, ret,
 				     "Couldn't register pinctrl driver\n");
 
+	/*
+	 * Bring-up diagnostic: what state did the bootloader leave the pogo
+	 * keyboard's pins in, before any driver has touched them?  The final
+	 * states are known to match the stock kernel (tests 055/064); whether
+	 * this probe - or anything before it - passes through a state the
+	 * keyboard's MCU never sees under stock is the one host-controlled
+	 * question left (P3 of the plan, tests 075-079).
+	 */
+	{
+		static const unsigned int watch[] = { 10, 12, 13, 62, 72, 75, 106 };
+		unsigned int g, k, w;
+
+		for (g = 0; g < soc_data->ngroups; g++) {
+			const struct msm_pingroup *grp = &soc_data->groups[g];
+
+			for (k = 0; k < grp->grp.npins; k++) {
+				for (w = 0; w < ARRAY_SIZE(watch); w++) {
+					if (grp->grp.pins[k] != watch[w])
+						continue;
+					dev_info(&pdev->dev,
+						 "pogo pin %u (%s) at probe: ctl %#x io %#x\n",
+						 grp->grp.pins[k], grp->grp.name,
+						 readl(pctrl->regs[grp->tile] + grp->ctl_reg),
+						 readl(pctrl->regs[grp->tile] + grp->io_reg));
+				}
+			}
+		}
+	}
+
 	for (i = 0; i < soc_data->nfunctions; i++) {
 		func = &soc_data->functions[i];
 
